{"title":"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d853f4f81efccb21abd89acd376700c5fd052d7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n,p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> of positive integers such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a prime, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> not exceeded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/c/72c9925c5c9c964c4a3ab50d7516202c1e614310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/5574c5b45b17fbbd05d53a116631c97f1556ba55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p-1)^{n}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/7/2f76a76d3184d8cd583de92d3b88226b364edba9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{p-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>official solution \nClearly we have the solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/10806bcbd66c9aaf6cfaaadf23b27f7e9e148cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2b596a120dcf60e33c7bfe19003bb1675bf37a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and for every other solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/9/75907a722d01dc0de9c68399ba686fbf9a67260c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. It remains to find the solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/57289ce83582f88bc50451f4eb39db66b23948ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/c/21cd6b8937bb07478e903e0186b41beefded34b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/9/75907a722d01dc0de9c68399ba686fbf9a67260c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. We claim that in this case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by p and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/3/273bed1a1db193e1fb3daee6595f8ee981bd5ffe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x y 2p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" />, whence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19a8531373871b279fc778aa78a17f0f88015206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" />. This will lead to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/c/5dcb92f1390234d96e36f164d0fd147d3ad72d49.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p^{p-1}|(p-1)^{p}+1=p^{2}\\left(p^{p-2}-{p \\choose 1}p^{p-3}+ \\cdots + -{p \\choose p-3}p-{p \\choose p-2}+1\\right)\\]\" width=\"592\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>therefore, because all the terms in the brackets excepting the last one is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/1/1617ca2d62a6c387bde76b439c462f44fd4e1d72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-1 \\leq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />. This leaves only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54cfc82a82f113a7432ca68f71338c383bbcb44b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/2/b022dc8ef6d33931fc1ae3d27df3ea0a81b52936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Let us prove now the claim. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/c/50c011fc3d9aa8f800963807b507b235b5aea34a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p-1)^{x}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" /> is odd, so is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> (therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/165d72eead4e5a9622816b17976f7165e6cbb1ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 2p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" />). Denote by q the smallest prime divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/0/3801bdc8ea82b7785fd7bf19408c755274b33cd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q|(p-1)^{x}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/669ca819f29700ee6046a074452b799d66700654.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p-1)^{x} \\equiv -1 \\pmod {q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/0/1206280985f77d9f6cff960b2c91ff6eda21f768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(q,p-q)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"20\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/8405c030776ecfe72a4a64d6e82afb5519644315.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,p-q)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" /> (from the choice of q) leads to the existence of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f03710a9ffbf0ecba4ae631d6f3bd28ff7f48f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u,v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8363a7b936576a2b968aea9dff4f89363d832f9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ux+v(q-1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"20\" />, whence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cad4df650d1d7db5790c2f847422f23371ca25ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-1 \\equiv (p-1)^{ux}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/0/ff0a4600ef4a8feef91df1c5a5f953b21b3a7e32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p-1)^{v(q-1)} \\equiv (-1)^{u} \\cdot 1^{v} \\equiv -1 \\pmod {q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"318\" height=\"23\" />, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be odd. This shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74fd4e027a8339c816aa0eb6e73e88e891ed4ce1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q|p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/891d3debca0eb4fc748577a63ec54a77fafa8f70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />. In conclusion the required solutions are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bdafca7228d0d0ab05e65bb872a9eb155393b3d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,2), (3,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/10806bcbd66c9aaf6cfaaadf23b27f7e9e148cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is an arbitrary prime.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO\" title=\"1999 IMO\">1999 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017005332\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 225/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6859/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.259      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.259      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25412:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017005332 and revision id 268555. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}